The sound effects are notes and priority, in that order:
  "select" has "84:1 96:1" and 1.
  "bump" has "noise:1 42:1" and 1.
  "hit" has "noise:2 45:1 38:2" and 2.
  "heal" has "72:1 76:1 79:1 84:3" and 3.
  "badge" has "72:2 76:2 79:2 84:4 79:2 84:6" and 3.
  "faint" has "67:1 63:1 60:1 55:3" and 3.
  "encounter" has "noise:1 0:1 79:1 84:1 79:1 84:2" and 2.
  "item" has "72:1 76:1 79:1 84:2" and 1.
  "victory" has "72:1 72:1 72:1 72:3 68:3 70:3 72:1 0:1 70:1 72:5" and 3.

To play a title (text):
  If Score's music is not the title:
    Set Score's music to the title.
    Let the score title be the title.
    If the title is "battle":
      Set the score title to "trainer".
    Let the score sheet be the scores for the score title.
    Set Score's tempo to the score sheet's tempo or else Score's tempo.
    Set Score's melody to the score sheet's melody or else "".
    Set Score's intro melody to the score sheet's intro melody or else "".
    Set Score's harmony to the score sheet's harmony or else "".
    Set Score's intro harmony to the score sheet's intro harmony or else "".
    Set Score's bass to the score sheet's bass or else "".
    Set Score's intro bass to the score sheet's intro bass or else "".
    Set Score's intro percussion to the score sheet's intro percussion or else "".
    Set Score's percussion to the score sheet's percussion or else "".

To sound a title (text):
  Let the effect sheet be the sound effects for the title.
  Set Score's effect to the effect sheet's notes or else "".
  Set Score's effect priority to the effect sheet's priority or else 1.
  Add 1 to Score's effect count.
  Now Score is cued.
